# Third-Party Licenses

The licenses of every Rust dependency compiled into the `steins` release binary,
so a binary-only distribution carries the notices those licenses require.

Steins's own terms are **not** here — the core is Apache-2.0 (ADR-0025) and its
license text is [`LICENSE`](LICENSE). PHPStan's MIT license is likewise not
here — PHPStan is Steins' direct model (see the README's "Acknowledgments"),
not a compiled Rust dependency, so this generated file never discovers it; its
text is [`LICENSE-PHPSTAN`](LICENSE-PHPSTAN). Dev-only crates (test tooling,
never linked into a shipped binary) are excluded.

_Generated by `cargo xtask licenses` (`cargo about generate about.hbs`); do not
edit by hand. Entries are grouped by license text — each distinct license body
appears once, with the list of crates that use it._

